  "job_B1.3.29_20251001_193211": {
    "text": "VII IDUS OCTOBR, PASSIO SANCTI DIONISII ET SOCIORUM EIUS.\nPAULUS, \u00d0EODA LAREOW, \u00fea \u00f0a he geond land ferde bodigende geleafan swa swa him bebead se\n\u00de\u00e6r w\u00e6s Dionisius, se deorwur\u00f0a martyr, \u00fe\u00e6ra h\u00e6\u00feena lareow on heora geleafleaste, o\u00fe \u00fe\u00e6t Paulus hine\nSe Dyonisius geseah, mid sumum o\u00ferum u\u00f0witan, on egypta lande \u00fe\u00e6r hi \u00e6t lare w\u00e6ron, hu seo sunne\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Dyonisius, \u00feeos deorce niht getacna\u00fe micel leoht towerd eallum middanearde \u00fe\u00e6t God sylf\nHe w\u00e6s \u00fea iung mann, \u00fea \u00f0a \u00feis gewear\u00f0, and him com \u00fe\u00e6t leoht to, \u00feurh Paules lare sy\u00f0\u00f0an, swa swa\nPaulus eode \u00fea gleawlice and heora godas sceawode ealle be endebyrdnysse, and eac \u00fea weofoda, o\u00fe\n\u00dea bewende hine Paulus to Dionisie \u00feam Drihtnes men and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Hw\u00e6t is se uncu\u00f0a god \u00fee ge\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Dyonisius, he is digle git mannum, and is towerd on worulde, and gewylt ealle \u00feing, heofonas\n\u00d0a andwyrde Paulus, hw\u00e6t \u00feinc\u00f0 eow be \u00feam gode, bi\u00fe he gast o\u00f0\u00f0e man?\nDyonisius andwyrde \u00feam arwur\u00f0an Paule \u00feus, He bi\u00f0 so\u00f0lice God, and so\u00f0lice man, and he sylf\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se halga Paulus, \u00feone God ic eow bodige \u00feone \u00f0e ge hata\u00f0 uncu\u00f0ne; he is acenned of Marian\nHe astah eac to heofonum to his halgan f\u00e6der, and sitt on his swi\u00f0ran hand, so\u00f0 God, and so\u00f0 man,\n\u00dea \u00f0a Paulus \u00fe\u00e6r lange d\u00e6ges geleafan \u00fe\u00e6r bodode, \u00fea gelyfde Dyonisius on \u00feone lifigendan God, and\nHe b\u00e6d \u00fea georne Paulum \u00fe\u00e6t he him geb\u00e6de fore \u00feone mildheortan Drihten, \u00fe\u00e6t he his discipulus\nEft on \u00feam o\u00ferum d\u00e6ge eode Paulus be \u00fe\u00e6re str\u00e6t, and gemette \u00e6nne blindne mann, se w\u00e6s geboren\n\u00dea eode se geh\u00e6leda, gehyrsum \u00feam apostole, and bead his h\u00e6sa bealdlice Dyonisie.\nDyonisius \u00fea axode \u00feone \u00e6rendracan, ofwundrod, eart \u00feu la se blinda \u00fee swa geboren w\u00e6re?\nHe andwyrde sona \u00feam arwur\u00fean were, Ic eom se ylca \u00fee \u00feu embe sprycst, \u00fee blind w\u00e6s geboren, and\nDionisius \u00fea aras, and hra\u00f0e efste to Paule mid eallum his hiwum to \u00f0am halgan fulluhte, and wear\u00f0\nDionisius \u00fea wunode, deoplice gel\u00e6red, on \u00fe\u00e6re fores\u00e6dan byrig \u00e6t his bisceopstole, and bodode \u00feam\nHe gebigde \u00fea \u00fea burhware to Gode, and \u00feone m\u00e6stan d\u00e6l \u00fe\u00e6s mancynnes to geleafan and fela bec\nSum \u00fe\u00e6ra hatte Titus, sum Timotheus, sum Policarpus, and gehwilce o\u00fere.\nEac to Iohanne, \u00feam arwur\u00f0an godspellere, he sende gewritu \u00fea \u00fea he on wr\u00e6csi\u00f0e w\u00e6s on Pathmo\nDionisius hine gefrefrode mid forewitegunge \u00fea and s\u00e6de \u00fe\u00e6t he wiste \u00fea gewislice \u00feurh God, \u00fe\u00e6t\nDionisius \u00fea ferde geond fela burga gehwider, and geond land bodigende bealdlice geleafan, and\n\u00dea wolde Dionisius, gif hit gewur\u00f0an mihte, \u00ferowian martyrdom mid \u00feam apostolum, and gewende \u00fea\nHit gelamp \u00f0a swa, for his langsumum f\u00e6re, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea halgan apostolas, swa swa se h\u00e6lend wolde,\nHe com \u00fea \u00e6t nextan si\u00f0\u00f0an se casere Nero his lif geendode earmlicum dea\u00f0e, and w\u00e6s Clemens papa\n\u00dea wunode se bisceop binnan Rome byrig mid Clemente papan cu\u00f0lice sume hwile, o\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t Clemens\nFar nu on Godes naman to Francena rice, swa swa Cristes cempa, mid cenum geleafan, and beo \u00fee\nIc cwe\u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu underfo eall Francena rice to \u00feinre bodunge, and beo Crist sylf mid \u00f0e, swa hwider\nNe wanda \u00feu nateshwon for \u00fean w\u00e6lhreowan folce; swa man swi\u00f0or swinc\u00f0, swa man selran mede\nHe funde him \u00fea geferan, and he ferde gebyld \u00feurh \u00feone halgan gast, \u00feam h\u00e6\u00f0enum bodigende\nHe gebohte \u00fea land \u00e6t anum geleaffullan men, and \u00fe\u00e6r cyrcan ar\u00e6rde hra\u00f0e mid cr\u00e6fte and Godes\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea Dionisius d\u00e6ghwamlice gebigde fela to geleafan mid his f\u00e6geran lare, and his Drihtne\nSwa fela wundra worhte se ealwealdenda God \u00feurh \u00feone halgan wer, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea wundra gebigdon \u00fea\nHe sende his geferan sume to Ispaniam, and to o\u00f0rum landum, Godes lare to sawenne, and he sylf\nGelome \u00fea h\u00e6\u00f0engildan, \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6r heteloste w\u00e6ron, gesamnodon heora gegadan and ceaste astyrodon,\nAc swa hra\u00f0e swa hi gesawon his scinendan nebwlite mid \u00feam heofonlican leohte, \u00feonne ledon \u00fea\nWundorlic Godes gifu, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feam w\u00e6penleasan menn ne mihton \u00fea w\u00e6lhreowan mid w\u00e6pnum\nWurdon \u00fea tobrocene, wide geond \u00fe\u00e6t land, \u00fe\u00e6ra h\u00e6\u00feenra Goda hus and anlicnyssa \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6ra manna\nSe ealde deofol \u00fee is mid andan afylled nam micelne graman ongean \u00feone Godes man for \u00fe\u00e6s folces\n\u00d0a wurdon \u00e6t nextan \u00fea w\u00e6lhreowan h\u00e6\u00feengildan mid teonan astyrode, swa swa hi tihte se deofol,\n\u00deis gewrit com \u00f0a to \u00feam casere on Rome, and he wear\u00f0 sona wodlice astyrod, swa \u00fe\u00e6t he het\nHe sende eac sona sumne heahgerefan Sisinnius gehaten, swi\u00f0e hetel deofol, mid manegum geferum\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea Sisinnius mid swi\u00f0licum prasse ferde, o\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he to \u00fe\u00e6re byrig com \u00fe\u00e6r se bisceop on w\u00e6s\n\u00dea het se w\u00e6lhreowa \u00feone halgan wer gebindan, and \u00e6nne m\u00e6ssepreost \u00fee he him mid funde,\n\u00deas halgan weras \u00e6fre wunodon mid \u00feam bisceope, o\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t hi tog\u00e6dere ealle to Gode ferdon.\n\u00dea axode Sisinnius mid swi\u00f0licum \u00fereate \u00feone halgan wer sona hwylcne God he wur\u00f0ode.\nHi cw\u00e6don \u00fea ealle \u00fery swilce mid anum mu\u00f0e, We andetta\u00f0 mid mu\u00f0e and on mode gelyfa\u00f0 on \u00fea\nSisinnius \u00f0a cw\u00e6\u00f0, secga\u00fe gif ge willa\u00f0 \u00feam casere gehyrsumian, and on his godas gelyfan, gif ge\nHe het \u00f0a \u00feone halgan bisceop unscrydan, and unm\u00e6\u00f0lice swingan, and he sang his gebeda betwux\nEft \u00fea Sisinnius het swingan \u00feone m\u00e6ssepreost, and eac \u00feone diacon, Dionisies geferan, and het hi\nHe het hi eft swingan, and si\u00f0\u00f0an \u00feone bisceop on isenum bedde astrehte, and byrnenda gleda dyde\n\u00dea het se w\u00e6lhreowa hine wurpan deorum \u00fee w\u00e6ron ofhingrode \u00fe\u00e6t hi \u00feone halgan wer abiton, ac \u00fea\n\u00dea het se dema awurpan \u00feone Drihtnes \u00f0\u00e6gen into byrnendum ofne, ac his gebedu adwescton ealne\nGit \u00fea se w\u00e6lhreowa dema het wyrcan ane hencgene, and het hon \u00feone bisceop to bismore \u00fe\u00e6ron, and\n\u00dea het se dema eft don hine of \u00fe\u00e6re hencgene, and l\u00e6dan hi ealle \u00fery to leohtleasum cwearterne, and\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a se bisceop bli\u00f0elice tihte mid lare \u00fea Cristenan on \u00feam cwearterne to Gode, and him eallum\n\u00de\u00e6r com eac se H\u00e6lend mid \u00feam heofonlican leohte, and fela engla mid him, \u00fe\u00e6r menn onlocodon,\nOngin nu stranglice, and \u00fein gemynd stent on heorunge, seo lufu and welwillendnys \u00fee wuna\u00f0 on\nSisinnius eft het sona \u00fe\u00e6s on mergen gefeccan \u00fea halgan of \u00feam fulum cwearterne, and het geoffrian\n\u00dea halgan \u00fea \u00feurhwunodon on \u00f0\u00e6s H\u00e6lendes geleafan, and se woda dema wolde \u00fea git cunnian, gif he\n\u00dea l\u00e6ddon \u00fea h\u00e6\u00f0enan \u00fea halgan to sl\u00e6ge, and Dionisius \u00feancode his Drihtne mid herunge ealra \u00fe\u00e6ra\n\u00de\u00e6r com \u00fea micel leoht to \u00fe\u00e6ra martyra lice, and \u00fe\u00e6s bisceopes lic mid \u00feam leohte aras, and nam his\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a h\u00e6\u00feenan, \u00fea \u00fee gehyrdon \u00feone sang and \u00fe\u00e6t wundor gesawon, awurpon heora gedwyld, and\n\u00de\u00e6t w\u00e6s syllic wundor \u00fe\u00e6t se so\u00f0f\u00e6sta martyr heafodleas mihte gan, God \u00e6lmihtigne herigende, and\nSisinnius swa\u00feeah, se unges\u00e6liga dema, nolde on Crist gelyfan, ac het acwellan ealle \u00fee \u00feurh\n\u00de\u00e6s halgan preostes lic and \u00fe\u00e6s geleaffullan diacones, Rusticus and Eleutherius, lagon uppan \u00fe\u00e6re\n\u00dea b\u00e6ron \u00fea h\u00e6\u00f0enan cwelleras \u00fe\u00e6ra halgena lic sona to scipe woldon hi besencan on flode, ac se\nSum \u00e6\u00feelboren wif w\u00e6s \u00fee wiste heora unr\u00e6d, and gela\u00f0ode \u00fea cwelleras swilce for cy\u00f0\u00f0e hire to,\nEft si\u00f0\u00fean on fyrste feng \u00fe\u00e6t Cristene folc to and worhton m\u00e6re mynster ofer \u00fe\u00e6ra martyra lic, \u00fe\u00e6r hi\n\u00de\u00e6r beo\u00fe fela wundra geworhte gelome \u00feurh \u00fea halgan martyras mannum to frofre, \u00fe\u00e6r underfo\u00f0 \u00fea",
